## Flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/apps/erts/erl_cmd.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here.

## Schedulers: a few, and none of them spinning.
##
## The daemon's work is waiting — on HTTP, on the felt and tmux subprocesses it
## shells out to, on files — so a handful of schedulers carry it on every host,
## a laptop or a many-core login node alike. Left to the defaults, the VM sizes
## its thread pools to the machine's logical CPUs (128 on an HPC login node,
## whatever cgroup quota actually applies) and each idle scheduler busy-waits
## before sleeping. On a shared login node that spin is most of the daemon's
## CPU time, and CPU time is what a per-process limit kills it for.
##
##   +S 2:2       two normal schedulers, both online
##   +SDcpu 2:2   two dirty-CPU schedulers (JSON and TLS bursts are short)
##   +SDio 4      four dirty-IO schedulers for file operations, which the
##                poller issues in bursts across every store
##   +sbwt*       no busy-wait on any scheduler class: an idle thread sleeps
##                at once, trading microseconds of wake-up latency the daemon
##                cannot notice for CPU it would otherwise burn.
+S 2:2
+SDcpu 2:2
+SDio 4
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
